</div>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Write an equivalent expression in the form of squared factors.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>Squared factors: \((2x−7)^2\).</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Solve the equation \(4x^2−28x=-33\) by completing the square. Show your reasoning.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{aligned} 4 x^{2}-28 x &amp;=-33 \\ 4 x^{2}-28 x+49 &amp;=-33+49 \\ (2 x-7)^{2} &amp;=16 \\ \sqrt{(2 x-7)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{16} \\ 2 x-7 &amp;=4 \\ 2 x-7 &amp;=-4 \\ 2 x &amp;=11 \\ 2 x &amp;=3 \end{aligned}\)</para>
  <para class="os-raise-noindent"> \(x=\frac{11}{2} \text { and } x=\frac{3}{2}\) </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
